{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He became the Count of Tripoli after his father was murdered in 1152. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem his father was the Count of Tripoli and his mother was a princess of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli after his father was murdered in 1152 he was around 12 years old at that time. He was under the regency of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem until he came of age. \n*Marriage and Children* \nRaymond III married Hodierna of Jerusalem's niece also named Hodierna but the marriage was childless. \n*Relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem* \nRaymond III had a complex relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was the grandson of Baldwin II of Jerusalem and the cousin of Baldwin IV of Jerusalem. \n*Siege of Tripoli* \nIn 1187 Saladin besieged Tripoli but Raymond III was able to defend the city successfully. \n*Battle of Hattin* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Crusader army was defeated by Saladin. He advised the Crusader army to avoid battle but his advice was not taken. \n*Later Life* \nAfter the Battle of Hattin Raymond III retired to Tripoli where he died in 1187. He was the last Count of Tripoli from the House of Toulouse. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III was a significant figure in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was known for his military skills and his complex relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.00091165461344644